WEBVTT

00:25.250 --> 00:32.210
<b>Beyond Journey's End</b>

01:29.980 --> 01:32.980
Episode 31: Somewhere She'd Like

01:32.980 --> 01:36.980
<b>29 years after the death of Himmel the Hero,
in the Etwas Mountains, located in the northern lands</b>

01:44.600 --> 01:47.820
It's gotten warm lately.

01:47.820 --> 01:50.100
This is a volcanic area.

01:50.100 --> 01:53.200
It's an unusually warm region 
within the northern lands.

01:53.200 --> 01:56.220
Which means we can finally 
enjoy some hot springs.

01:56.710 --> 02:01.280
That's right. We'll probably 
arrive at the next village soon.

02:01.280 --> 02:03.400
We can take a dip there.

02:18.330 --> 02:22.370
Hey, Frieren. We've been 
walking for a while.

02:22.670 --> 02:24.330
Are we there yet?

02:26.620 --> 02:29.870
The village should be around here.

02:33.720 --> 02:35.750
I see a cabin.

02:37.220 --> 02:39.010
Just one building.

02:39.330 --> 02:41.270
I have a bad feeling about this.

02:45.350 --> 02:47.070
Wait, mister!

02:47.070 --> 02:48.970
Hurry up!

02:49.510 --> 02:51.130
Wait for me!

02:51.940 --> 02:54.150
This brings back memories.

02:54.480 --> 02:59.160
The village was abandoned 
over thirty years ago.

03:00.400 --> 03:05.070
The hot spring dried up, so the 
adventurers stopped coming.

03:04.410 --> 03:05.900
One at a time!

03:05.900 --> 03:08.510
That's a shame, isn't it, Ms. Frieren?

03:12.160 --> 03:16.220
Human villages always vanish the 
moment you let your guard down.

03:16.860 --> 03:20.350
We'll have to wait until the next town 
to enjoy the hot springs.

03:21.180 --> 03:23.550
How far is it to the next town?

03:24.070 --> 03:25.980
About a week's journey.

03:26.490 --> 03:29.050
So we have to wait a whole week.

03:31.050 --> 03:33.850
Are there no other 
hot springs around here?

03:36.580 --> 03:38.070
Come to think of it,

03:38.490 --> 03:41.210
I heard from my grandfather

03:41.210 --> 03:45.080
that there's a hidden hot spring 
in the mountains back there.

03:46.580 --> 03:51.160
That was over thirty years ago, though.

03:52.320 --> 03:54.430
It's the hidden hot spring 
of the Etwas Mountains.

03:55.710 --> 03:57.350
You're familiar with it?

03:57.800 --> 04:00.590
I doubt it's still there.

04:00.590 --> 04:02.950
It's pretty deep in the mountains.

04:02.950 --> 04:08.230
We'd probably reach a hot spring sooner 
by just heading to the next town.

04:09.930 --> 04:12.500
What is it, Mr. Stark?

04:13.000 --> 04:15.430
The hidden hot spring of 
the Etwas Mountains...

04:15.430 --> 04:17.830
I feel like I've heard those words before.

04:19.750 --> 04:22.310
Oh, I remember now.

04:22.310 --> 04:27.080
Frieren, I think I'd like to visit 
the hidden hot spring.

04:27.390 --> 04:28.590
Mr. Stark?

04:29.030 --> 04:35.420
Stark, even though it's technically a hot 
spring, it's really not worth the trouble.

04:35.420 --> 04:36.290
After all, it's—

04:36.290 --> 04:39.520
We came all the way here already. 
Let's go check it out.

04:45.740 --> 04:50.410
Fine. If you really want to go, let's go.

04:51.100 --> 04:54.090
Later, mister!

04:54.090 --> 04:56.610
Let's play again!

04:56.610 --> 04:58.600
Later!

05:46.200 --> 05:48.440
We're almost at the hidden hot spring.

05:53.960 --> 05:58.510
Ms. Frieren, you don't seem very excited.

05:58.510 --> 05:59.780
I guess not.

05:59.780 --> 06:02.350
I wandered through the mountains

06:02.350 --> 06:04.970
in search of the hidden hot spring 
with Himmel and the others.

06:07.670 --> 06:09.360
I want to go home.

06:09.360 --> 06:10.430
Me, too.

06:11.560 --> 06:15.470
You traveled there with 
Mr. Himmel's party, too?

06:15.940 --> 06:22.940
Himmel wasn't satisfied until he searched 
every nook and cranny of an unusual place.

06:23.480 --> 06:26.980
You said it'd be quick!

06:26.980 --> 06:29.480
I'm telling you, there's something here.

06:30.030 --> 06:32.750
I can feel it in my gut.

06:33.580 --> 06:35.350
I told you so.

06:35.350 --> 06:37.400
There's no turning back now.

06:38.810 --> 06:42.500
The road to the hidden hot spring 
is especially brutal.

06:45.750 --> 06:49.570
You have to pass through the territory 
of a troublesome monster.

07:03.260 --> 07:05.420
It's here already.

07:05.420 --> 07:06.400
Let's do this.

07:18.650 --> 07:19.920
A dragon, huh?

07:19.920 --> 07:21.770
It's been a while.

07:21.770 --> 07:23.510
That's not a dragon.

07:23.510 --> 07:27.480
If anything, that monster 
is closer to being a lizard.

07:27.480 --> 07:28.790
A lizard?

07:30.110 --> 07:32.920
It's quite agitated.

07:32.920 --> 07:36.560
That's typical of monsters 
when their territory is invaded.

07:37.040 --> 07:41.070
You have to cut off all three heads at 
the same time, or they'll regenerate.

07:41.070 --> 07:42.690
Seriously?!

07:54.890 --> 07:56.460
Run, Stark.

07:57.470 --> 07:59.190
I have a plan.

07:59.570 --> 08:00.990
What kind of—

08:17.490 --> 08:20.900
We'll split up to the left and right 
and attack all three heads at once.

08:20.900 --> 08:21.690
Understood.

08:22.050 --> 08:24.770
Let's do this in as few 
attempts as possible.

08:25.560 --> 08:29.440
If our timing is off, 
it'll keep regenerating.

08:29.440 --> 08:30.500
Um...

08:31.600 --> 08:34.120
The plan you mentioned earlier...

08:34.840 --> 08:38.750
We'll strike while the monster 
is attacking Stark.

08:42.090 --> 08:43.330
You mean...

08:51.480 --> 08:53.900
I was just the bait.

08:57.320 --> 08:59.950
Good work, both of you.

09:41.930 --> 09:44.020
We're finally here.

09:44.020 --> 09:45.520
That was difficult.

09:46.110 --> 09:50.350
See? I told you we should've just 
headed to the next town.

09:51.410 --> 09:53.970
That's the hidden hot spring 
of the Etwas Mountains.

10:07.300 --> 10:08.800
It's so shallow.

10:10.180 --> 10:12.310
This is just a foot bath.

10:12.310 --> 10:15.050
I told you it wasn't worth the effort.

10:16.090 --> 10:17.920
This is fine.

10:21.490 --> 10:23.780
This way, we can all enjoy it together.

10:29.190 --> 10:30.650
You're right.

10:41.450 --> 10:43.250
This is a nice view.

10:43.850 --> 10:44.860
Yeah.

10:46.190 --> 10:50.510
By the way, Mr. Stark, 
why did you want to come here?

10:51.230 --> 10:53.720
I heard about it from my master.

10:54.120 --> 10:58.710
The hidden hot spring of the Etwas 
Mountains was just a foot bath.

10:58.710 --> 11:01.450
It wasn't worth the effort at all.

11:01.450 --> 11:04.020
It was a truly ridiculous adventure.

11:05.560 --> 11:08.350
It's strange, though.

11:09.080 --> 11:12.670
I wouldn't trade my memories

11:12.670 --> 11:16.640
of those ridiculous adventures 
with my friends for anything.

11:21.070 --> 11:23.830
<i>I'll never forget that view.</i>

11:30.700 --> 11:32.990
So you knew, Mr. Stark.

11:34.390 --> 11:37.880
I think I wanted to see the 
same view my master saw.

11:44.980 --> 11:47.470
It really is a nice view.

12:10.420 --> 12:12.900
The way back is brutal, too.

12:18.360 --> 12:22.140
Maybe it wasn't worth 
the effort after all.

12:23.050 --> 12:28.050
<b>29 years after the death
of Himmel the Hero,
in the fortress city of Heiß,
located in the northern lands</b>

12:35.500 --> 12:40.310
You sure love hot springs 
for someone so young.

12:52.200 --> 12:53.830
Yeah!

12:52.200 --> 12:53.830
Dang it!

12:53.830 --> 12:55.210
Next game!

12:58.970 --> 13:04.330
Ms. Frieren has been soaking in the 
hot springs ever since we arrived here.

13:04.330 --> 13:07.720
When she does come out, 
it's just to visit magic shops.

13:08.580 --> 13:11.210
Apparently, we're staying 
for two more days.

13:11.550 --> 13:14.630
I guess that's a short stay for Frieren.

13:14.630 --> 13:16.600
I made sure to give her an earful.

13:17.560 --> 13:20.470
We have nothing to do 
all day tomorrow, though.

13:20.940 --> 13:22.530
You're right.

13:22.530 --> 13:24.890
Maybe I'll visit a weapon shop.

13:24.890 --> 13:26.460
I need to get my axe sharpened.

13:26.460 --> 13:29.420
Okay, but <i>I'll</i> have nothing 
to do all day tomorrow.

13:33.980 --> 13:35.450
Pay attention to me.

13:38.830 --> 13:42.590
You're so inconsiderate, Mr. Stark.

13:42.590 --> 13:47.130
Seriously? You didn't 
have to put it like that.

13:48.150 --> 13:50.860
<i>She's always so hard on me.</i>

13:51.660 --> 13:54.880
<i>Fine. It's time for some payback.</i>

13:56.590 --> 14:00.020
If you're that desperate for attention, 
let's go on a date tomorrow.

14:06.670 --> 14:09.240
<i>Oops. This never goes well.</i>

14:13.890 --> 14:15.290
<i>I'm dead.</i>

14:18.800 --> 14:21.810
Very well. See you tomorrow.

14:36.020 --> 14:39.810
Um, your book...

14:43.760 --> 14:45.450
<i>Why'd she react like that?</i>

14:57.650 --> 14:59.300
Excuse me...

15:13.470 --> 15:15.400
Frieren...

15:18.350 --> 15:22.470
What do you think? Is she mad?

15:23.060 --> 15:25.320
What's going to happen to me?

15:25.680 --> 15:30.050
Stark, do you understand 
who you're asking for advice?

15:30.050 --> 15:31.280
Have you lost your mind?

15:31.740 --> 15:35.150
You're right. Sorry for 
asking the impossible.

15:35.150 --> 15:37.600
I never said it was impossible.

15:37.600 --> 15:39.810
I'm a grown woman, you know.

15:39.810 --> 15:42.020
I know exactly how a girl thinks.

15:42.720 --> 15:45.660
Are you sure? I'm trusting you.

15:46.620 --> 15:48.500
Okay, let me ask you again.

15:48.500 --> 15:52.870
Frieren, if I said to you, "Let's go 
on a date," what would you think?

15:53.560 --> 15:56.100
You've grown into a fine man, Stark.

15:56.100 --> 15:58.860
I'm so happy, I might treat you to dinner.

15:58.860 --> 16:01.850
Yeah, this isn't helping.

16:01.850 --> 16:05.310
This feels like a grandma 
hanging out with her grandson.

16:06.100 --> 16:07.890
You just called me a grandma.

16:07.890 --> 16:10.080
That's your second offense 
after calling me a hag.

16:10.080 --> 16:11.380
You won't get away with a third.

16:11.380 --> 16:13.360
Why are you counting? You're scaring me!

16:13.670 --> 16:16.490
By the way, what happens 
on the third offense?

16:16.490 --> 16:18.280
I'll scream and cry.

16:18.280 --> 16:21.190
My tantrums are scary, you know.

16:21.190 --> 16:24.300
They even made Himmel the Hero 
tremble with fear.

16:41.880 --> 16:44.530
She's been crying for three 
full days and nights.

16:44.530 --> 16:45.550
Yikes.

16:45.550 --> 16:46.600
Terrifying.

16:46.860 --> 16:48.490
That sounds terrifying.

16:48.490 --> 16:51.030
Is that how a grown woman behaves?

16:54.730 --> 16:59.290
Well, I understand now that you're 
entirely lacking in tact and sensitivity.

17:01.290 --> 17:03.690
So, are you going on a date with Fern?

17:05.620 --> 17:09.390
It doesn't feel like 
I can take it back now.

17:09.390 --> 17:13.490
So I thought I'd ask you to suggest 
some places she might like.

17:15.320 --> 17:18.000
Actually, never mind. 
I shouldn't have asked—

17:18.000 --> 17:19.380
Should we go take a look, then?

17:19.380 --> 17:20.250
What?

17:20.250 --> 17:21.920
I can probably find somewhere.

17:23.440 --> 17:24.850
Somewhere she'd like.

17:25.780 --> 17:27.070
What should we do now?

17:27.070 --> 17:28.440
Why don't we get something to eat?

17:28.440 --> 17:29.410
Good idea.

17:29.620 --> 17:32.680
You should start by getting her 
something to eat at the market.

17:33.190 --> 17:35.960
She gets cranky when she's hungry.

17:37.280 --> 17:39.180
Don't skip the food stalls.

17:39.680 --> 17:42.980
Fern has loved snacking 
since she was little.

17:46.430 --> 17:50.830
She'd probably like shops 
with pretty items on display.

17:51.740 --> 17:56.750
Fern likes baked goods, but what 
she wants depends on her mood,

17:57.670 --> 18:01.580
so you should choose a few dessert shops.

18:07.490 --> 18:09.050
What else...

18:15.870 --> 18:20.780
Quiet plazas like these 
are an option, too.

18:22.490 --> 18:26.080
Seriously? You know Fern really well.

18:26.080 --> 18:28.260
I'm impressed, Frieren.

18:28.260 --> 18:31.030
No, I don't know anything.

18:32.300 --> 18:34.060
I'm not impressive.

18:34.520 --> 18:36.610
Heiter was the impressive one.

18:38.280 --> 18:43.020
He talked about Fern's 
preferences all the time.

18:44.280 --> 18:46.940
"She gets cranky when she's hungry,"

18:46.940 --> 18:50.890
"she likes snacking," 
"she likes pretty things,"

18:51.750 --> 18:57.670
and "her preferences change depending on 
her mood" are all things Heiter taught me.

18:59.730 --> 19:05.710
Heiter seemed to want me to be 
a parental figure to Fern,

19:06.460 --> 19:11.670
but ultimately, I failed 
to discover anything she liked.

19:19.360 --> 19:23.130
But you remember all of that.

19:24.000 --> 19:27.710
I think you're a good parent to her.

19:30.520 --> 19:32.870
Come to think of it,

19:32.870 --> 19:37.750
we first celebrated Fern's birthday 
on the road in a place like this.

19:42.240 --> 19:45.040
You have some nice things 
to say sometimes, Stark.

19:45.810 --> 19:46.950
I know, right?

19:48.710 --> 19:51.610
I'll strike one offense from the record.

19:52.290 --> 19:53.630
Thanks...

20:19.410 --> 20:23.780
Ms. Frieren, I was asked out on a date.

20:24.370 --> 20:25.770
What should I do?

20:27.220 --> 20:28.740
You, too?

20:30.260 --> 20:32.250
It's nothing.

20:33.870 --> 20:37.370
Ms. Frieren, have you 
ever been on a date?

20:37.370 --> 20:38.640
I have.

20:38.640 --> 20:40.000
Of course you haven't.

20:42.110 --> 20:43.870
Wait, you have?!

20:44.080 --> 20:44.880
Yeah.

20:48.120 --> 20:51.670
Who did you go with, and what did you do?

20:52.240 --> 20:55.600
Himmel and I went looking for a lost cat.

20:56.010 --> 20:58.570
We were asked to by the owner 
of a magic item shop.

21:00.160 --> 21:02.970
So you were just completing a job.

21:03.410 --> 21:07.050
I'm not sure you can call that a date.

21:10.810 --> 21:12.560
Listen, Fern,

21:12.560 --> 21:16.020
when two close friends of opposing sex 
go out with each other and nobody else,

21:16.020 --> 21:18.430
that's a date.

21:21.350 --> 21:23.410
That's what my master said.

21:26.500 --> 21:29.700
Come to think of it, I went 
on a date with Sein, too.

21:29.700 --> 21:31.050
Forget it.

21:36.060 --> 21:37.480
Good night.

22:20.980 --> 22:25.110
Translation
Sho Stifler

